Or is it nine?

251
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:55,217
However many, it sure sounds
like you're in the zone.

252
00:12:55,300 --> 00:12:56,130
Huh.

253
00:12:56,860 --> 00:12:59,837
Don't think you're going to fool me
with your nice guy routine, Yugi.

254
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:01,477
It's only a matter of time before you...

255
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:04,157
Can't we just forget about
the tournament for one night?

256
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:05,917
Let's make fun of Joey instead.

257
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,057
That's always fun.

258
00:13:07,140 --> 00:13:11,500
Okay, just as long as everyone is
crystal clear about one little thing.

259
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:13,737
Any duelist in my way is going down.

260
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:14,900
Huh? Huh?

261
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:18,438
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I'm going to go for a walk.

262
00:13:18,740 --> 00:13:19,570
Huh?

263
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:26,160
Oh, man, she can really ruin a meal.

264
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:29,957
I should never have sat
down with those losers,

265
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:34,240
even if they do seem like kind
of nice losers and friendly.

266
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:37,700
And no, I can't afford to go soft now.

267
00:13:37,980 --> 00:13:41,257
I'm a duelist first, and that
means everyone is an enemy.

268
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:42,780
So no friends for me.

269
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:45,393
I want to win, and I'll do it all alone.

270
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,700
Man, oh, man.

271
00:13:58,520 --> 00:14:00,160
I'm fading fast here.

272
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:01,957
Don't you think we should check on Mai?

273
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:02,870
Good idea.

274
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,725
She has been gone for a while.

275
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:06,920
It's probably some trap. Hmm.

276
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:09,620
What was that?

277
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:11,770
Yep.

278
00:14:11,853 --> 00:14:13,257
Bet you she's been waiting
there the whole time.

279
00:14:13,340 --> 00:14:14,340
Come on out, Mai.

280
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:21,140
It's Akura. See? I told you.

281
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:23,540
I haven't just been seeing things.

282
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:28,017
What are you doing way out here, Bakura?

283
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:29,629
Same as you guys, I guess.

284
00:14:29,780 --> 00:14:32,177
You gave us a scare sneaking
around those bushes.

285
00:14:32,260 --> 00:14:36,257
Yeah, for a minute there, we actually
thought we had something to worry about.

286
00:14:36,340 --> 00:14:37,520
Pretty silly, huh?

287
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:42,657
Joey, you've been staring at
that card for like an hour.

288
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:43,570
What's up?

289
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,582
I'll tell you, just don't laugh.

290
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:47,525
Sometimes, when I'm in a duel,

291
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:50,197
I pretend that it's me
out there on the field

292
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:53,456
swapping blows with whatever
card my opponent has out.

293
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:54,760
Isn't that dumb?

294
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:58,473
Well, if you were, which card
would you want to be, Joey?

295
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,420
Uh, this one.

296
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:03,500
The Flame Swordsman
kicks everybody's butt.

297
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:06,100
Not my guys.

298
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:07,740
The Cyber Commander.

299
00:15:08,140 --> 00:15:10,297
You boys and your cards are hilarious.

300
00:15:10,380 --> 00:15:12,737
I think everyone has a card
they can identify with.

301
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:15,917
You should see if you can
pick one for yourself, Taya.

302
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:16,830
Okay.

303
00:15:16,913 --> 00:15:19,440
I picked this one,
Magician of Faith. What?

304
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:20,957
You gotta be kidding me.

305
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:23,457
More like the Magician
of Freaks, if you ask me.

306
00:15:23,540 --> 00:15:24,370
Shut up!

307
00:15:25,780 --> 00:15:28,251
Tell me which one you identify with, Yugi.

308
00:15:28,580 --> 00:15:29,620
Oh, that's easy.

309
00:15:29,740 --> 00:15:31,269
Dark Magician, hands down.

310
00:15:32,100 --> 00:15:33,637
Maybe I'm just out of the loop,

311
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:35,317
but don't you guys think
it's a little silly

312
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:37,777
to be comparing ourselves
to playing cards?

313
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:40,400
Maybe a little, but
it's like Grandpa says.

314
00:15:40,560 --> 00:15:41,837
It's not about the playing cards.

315
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:45,497
it's about putting a little bit of your
heart into anything that you care about,

316
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:46,410
you know?

317
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:49,497
So which card do you
care about most, Bakura?

318
00:15:49,580 --> 00:15:50,992
This one is my favorite.

319
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:55,957
Isn't that the change of heart card?

320
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:58,677
Kind of a weird-looking
picture, don't you think?

321
00:15:58,760 --> 00:15:59,590
Hmm.

322
00:15:59,673 --> 00:16:02,697
If you want to see how it works,
we could have a duel right now.

323
00:16:02,780 --> 00:16:05,260
Not for star chips, just for a little fun.

324
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:06,630
Sure.

325
00:16:06,713 --> 00:16:07,543
I'm down with that.

326
00:16:07,626 --> 00:16:09,037
After all the star chip stuff,

327
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:11,837
it'll be nice to have a duel
with no strings attached.

328
00:16:11,920 --> 00:16:12,750
I agree.

329
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:16,037
I think just a regular old
duel sounds like a great idea.

330
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:18,157
Why don't you guys each
put your favorite card

331
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:21,217
into Yuki's deck so it'll
be like we're all playing?

332
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:22,940
That's a good idea. Yeah.

333
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:26,817
Great, but I should warn you that
with this all-star team of cards,

334
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:28,237
we'll be tough to beat.

335
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:30,320
True, but maybe I'll surprise you.

336
00:16:30,580 --> 00:16:31,462
This'll be fun.

337
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:38,140
All right, I'm all shuffled.

338
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:40,677
Now you're sure you
don't mind playing alone?

339
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:42,917
Don't you worry about a thing, Bakura.

340
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,137
We'll go easy on you.

341
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:45,340
Thanks. Right.

342
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:47,697
Now let's get this duel on the road.

343
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:51,877
Before we get started, there's a little
something I'd like to share with you all.

344
00:16:51,960 --> 00:16:52,790
Huh?

345
00:16:52,873 --> 00:16:55,880
And especially with you,
Yugi. What's that? You'll see.

346
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:57,400
What's he doing?

347
00:16:58,260 --> 00:17:00,200
This is getting freaky.

348
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:03,700
No, it can't be.

349
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:05,020
A Millennium Item.

350
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:08,917
Yes, and the magic of my Millennium
Ring will take us to the Shadow Realm.

351
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,980
Man, I hate magic.

352
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:12,977
Why are you doing this, Bakura?

353
00:17:13,060 --> 00:17:16,860
You've something I want,
Yugi, and I aim to take it.

354
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:36,457
That wasn't too difficult.

355
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:42,060
Their souls have been locked away, and
now, after waiting for countless centuries,

356
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:44,840
the legendary Millennium Puzzle is mine.

357
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:53,430
No!

358
00:17:53,513 --> 00:17:54,660
It can't be!

359
00:17:55,060 --> 00:17:57,080
You want my Millennium Puzzle?

360
00:17:57,260 --> 00:17:59,637
Then you're going to
have to duel me for it.

361
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:03,417
But if I win, you'll release my
friends and send us all back!

362
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:08,340
I agree to your ridiculous
terms, Yugi, but I promise you,

363
00:18:08,620 --> 00:18:11,217
there is more at stake
here than you comprehend,

364
00:18:11,300 --> 00:18:15,240
and this is one shadow
game that you cannot win!
